> Feels complicated to modify all SendAsync call chains so they can return the endpoint

I was thinking we could try to extract it from the stream itself since these are all internals only.

E.g. something like
```c#
static IPEndPoint? GetRemoteEndPoint(Stream? stream)
{
    if (stream is HttpContentStream contentStream)
    {
        stream = contentStream._connection?._stream;
    }

    return (stream as NetworkStream)?.Socket?.RemoteEndPoint as IPEndPoint;
}
```

Since we know that (at least for now), a `CONNECT` request will be done over HTTP/1.1 without a TLS layer in between (assuming no `ConnectCallback`).

